# Optional: only needed if you want a trading account set up from this file
# (mainly for docker compose, where only the engine container reads .env) or
# "Import from .env" on the Accounts > API key tab. Everyone else sets up a
# trading account in the web UI instead (Account > Accounts: create, connect
# by signing, or paste an API key there) and can leave these two blank.
#
# Your MAIN Hyperliquid account address (the account that holds the money).
COPYCAT_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=0x...
# Private key of an API ("agent") wallet approved at https://app.hyperliquid.xyz/API.
# It can trade but cannot withdraw. NEVER put your main wallet's key here:
# copycat refuses a key whose address equals COPYCAT_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS.
# Only the engine reads this; under docker compose the api never receives it.
COPYCAT_AGENT_KEY=0x...
# Bearer token for the api (and the web UI login). At least 32 chars; "change-me" is rejected.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Or leave empty: the api generates one and writes it to $COPYCAT_DATA_DIR/api_token.
COPYCAT_API_TOKEN=
COPYCAT_BIND=127.0.0.1
COPYCAT_API_PORT=8787
COPYCAT_DATA_DIR=./data
# mainnet | testnet
COPYCAT_NETWORK=mainnet
# The browser origin the api accepts (CORS). Must match where you actually
# open the web UI, protocol and port included. Default http://localhost:3000
# is right for `make dev` / docker compose as shipped; only set this if you
# serve the web UI from somewhere else (a different port, a reverse proxy).
# `make dev WEB_PORT=...` sets this for you automatically; leave it unset.
# COPYCAT_WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
